WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.250
Jane, the wild girl who was raised by wolves.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:44.540
Unable to capture the essence of her sadness, her anger and her joy-the emotions of the lonely beast-

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.180
Maya went off alone to the mountains to find the wilderness within.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.080
Episode 42 - Counting on the Acting Festival

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:09.430
Maya, where the hell are you?!

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.310
I just couldn't get Jane down and before I knew what I was doing,

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.730
I'd caught the train and...

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.350
Sir, please give me some time!

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.860
I'd like to use this place to think about Jane.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:27.970
Okay, but remember: Part of an actor's worth is their body.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.910
Take good care of yourself.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.310
You got that, Kitajima?

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:36.400
Is it all right to let her run off like this?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.570
I wouldn't be able to stop her if I tried.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.570
And at the end of the day, you can't learn acting through rehearsals alone.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.860
She knows what she needs to do.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.760
You never cease to amaze me, Maya.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:55.800
There it is: Mt. Tengu. They say wolves once lived up there.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:04.050
When the sun goes down, I'll find a tree and stay under it for the night.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.840
Just like Jane.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:30.570
I wonder if this is how Jane hides from the lightning too.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.000
That was wonderful.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.050
I'm really looking forward to your opening night.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.280
We're going to clean up at the Acting Festival!

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.020
It's too bad for that wolf girl play, but our leading lady is in another league entirely!

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.220
I wonder if I should've taken the other path.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.180
Someone's there!

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:25.020
I see. So, you're doing this to help you with your part as a wolf.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.680
And what are you doing here, sir?

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.510
I'm a ranger.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.890
I'm here to protect the native animals from poachers.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:41.540
Then, you must see wild animals all the time!

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.640
Will you watch my acting for a bit?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.400
What do you mean by "acting"?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.450
Yeah... there's something not quite right about it.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.740
You look more like a city dog than a wild animal.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.220
It's the expression that's off; it's not wild at all.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.520
Well, I'll take you to the pass and then, you should head home.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.490
The sun will be setting soon.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.820
I can't go back.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.880
I haven't grasped the essence of Jane yet...

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:27.220
Not her heart, nor her wildness!

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.130
Wait!

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.650
Wow...

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:14.920
The sound of the birds...

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:17.530
The sound of the water...

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.650
This is Jane's world.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.540
It's so unbelievable.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.630
I feel like I'm floating in space.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:41.180
I like starry skies, the immensity of space.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.320
If I'm having a hard day, I can forget about it by coming here and looking up at all the stars.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.870
Thank you for joining me in this memory.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:57.600
Gross! Why did I think about <i>him</i>?

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.580
Why Mr. Hayami of all people?

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.790
What am I going to do?

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.570
I still don't have a hold on her.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:23.200
Jane's pain, her joy, her sadness at losing her older sister.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.730
I'm alive...

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.700
A wild face. Eyes that have no expression.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.760
This is her!

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:14.810
This is the wild Jane before she meets Stewart!

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:20.060
She promised she'd come back safe and sound!

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.760
Please, let me go look for her!

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:24.140
She's dear to me...

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.130
as a costar.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:45.510
I'm sorry for my lateness.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:49.430
Well, did you manage to get a grasp on Jane?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.500
Yes.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:56.350
Then, let's get on with the rehearsals. I'll reprimand you later.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.970
Welcome back, Jane.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.840
It's good to be back!

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:09.710
"For me, to live is to dance!"

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:12.920
"And to dance is to live!"

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:17.000
"This is my all!"

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:24.190
"But it's not simply that I wish to dance..."

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:27.380
"The rhythm controls the very beating of my heart!"

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.600
"I have no need of shoes! I'll show you all the true essence of dance!"

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:38.220
"Isadora Duncan was a forerunner of modern dance who shook up its world."

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.390
"Yet, her extraordinary life was leading her down a tragic path."

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:46.140
"Her children, whom she loved more than anything, died in an accident."

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.110
"Her partner, Yesenin, committed suicide."

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.760
"Why do you take all my light from me?"

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:57.370
"My children, spirited away by icy water!"

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.890
"And now you too, Yesenin!"

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:04.690
"I was a baby the first time I danced."

00:10:04.690 --> 00:10:08.840
"I'd flourish my arms and legs at the sound of music!"

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:13.470
"The only thing I have left now is the only thing I had back then: Dance."

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.430
"There's nothing else."

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.720
"Back then, I danced barefoot, and I'm still dancing barefoot now!"

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:24.560
"I'm still dancing now, but why? For what?"

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.250
"It's because I'm still alive!"

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.360
"Does it hurt to die?"

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.070
"Is it sad?"

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:33.960
"Is it frightening?"

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:37.970
"Or is it perhaps a happy event?"

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.130
"How should I dance?"

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:55.010
The play's over, Maya.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:55.790
Maya!

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.820
Your real show is yet to come.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:06.190
Use your own strength to grab your one percent chance!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:19.000
That was a very impressive show, Miss Enjouji.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:21.490
Thank you very much, Mr. President.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.230
How did you like it, Mr. Kuronuma?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.690
The singing and dancing were perfect.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.810
Thank you very much.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:35.230
Now, if only Isadora had more depth, it would have been even better.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.940
Are you saying that my acting was shallow?!

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:41.310
I'm very sorry, but I cannot lie.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:44.010
And what do you two think?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.190
I was really blown away by your singing and dancing!

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.740
It was wonderful.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:51.940
The lines really resonated with me!

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.790
Oh, which ones?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:57.880
Well, the scene in the bar was one.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:01.790
"For me, to live is to dance!"

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.630
"This is my all!"

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:07.750
"But it's not simply that I wish to dance..."

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:13.850
"The rhythm controls the very beating of my heart! The beating of my blood as it travels...

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:18.280
through each and every blood vessel and sways my whole body!"

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:21.980
"I find myself dancing all the time!"

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.270
I really loved that part!

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:27.610
You memorized all the lines?

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:29.030
Yes. Every last one of them!

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.870
All of them? Impossible!

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:38.370
Fine, whatever. What other parts did you like?

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:40.410
There are just too many,

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:44.120
but I guess if I had to pick one, the closing scene was very moving.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:48.010
What kind of scene was it? Recite it for us.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:54.170
Well? If you say you've memorized all the lines, then recite the scene.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:12.400
"I was a baby the first time I danced."

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:17.110
"I'd flourish my arms and legs at the sound of music!"

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:23.600
"The only thing I have left now is the only thing I had back then: Dance."

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.850
"There's nothing else."

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:29.590
"Back then, I danced barefoot, and I'm still dancing barefoot now!"

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:35.760
"I'm still dancing now, but why? For what?"

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.970
"It's because I'm still alive!"

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.130
"Does it hurt to die?"

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.870
"Is it sad?"

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.230
"Is it frightening?"

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:52.550
"Or is it perhaps a happy event?"

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.860
"How should I dance?"

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.260
This girl!

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:07.100
Thank you!

00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:12.950
You didn't play the end in the same way as Miss Enjouji.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.500
Why's that?

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.500
I'm not sure.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:19.570
Once I got into Isadora, that's just how it came out.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:24.260
Miss Enjouji played that part as someone who had become completely ground down by life.

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:27.100
You, on the other hand, looked like you had found...

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:30.170
your true dancing instinct amidst your suffering.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:34.560
You could never tell that this was an improvisation.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:40.950
We expect nothing less from Maya Kitajima, winner of the Acting Festival's Best Supporting Actress Award.

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:44.060
Your next piece is something about a wolf girl, isn't it?

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.110
Won't you show us a snippet of your role here?

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.430
What do you say?

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.090
Please, show us!

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:55.140
I'm sure you do a simply marvelous wolf girl!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:15:00.400
This is a chance to show off your acting to some of the Festival judges.

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:02.610
Let's go, Maya.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.010
Excuse us, we're leaving.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.430
You're running away?

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:08.650
You act out other people's roles, but you refuse to show your own?

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:12.240
You must not have enough confidence, Miss "Feral Dog" Jane.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:19.470
Maya, stop!

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:20.900
Stay out of this!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:24.000
I'll handle her.

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:30.460
Look, Jane... food!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.970
Look at her expression!

00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:40.830
Come!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.400
Wait!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.640
How can you do something like this, Mr. Masumi?

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.950
This is going to be hot!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.080
Right here, on the opening night of <i>Isadora</i>!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.480
The wolf girl and Masumi Hayami face off!

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:01.190
What was this play called again?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:03.110
<i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i> or something!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:05.010
What's going on?

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.970
This is <i>my</i> opening night!

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:12.030
Why aren't you coming to get your food, little wolf girl?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:15.050
That's it! That's the face!

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:19.170
"Jane... I am Jane!"

00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:25.910
That's good!

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:26.930
Jane!

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.840
Your food is over there!

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:35.320
What? Giving up already? You're running away with your tail between your legs?

00:16:37.170 --> 00:16:39.600
But you never had a tail to begin with!

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:14.300
I guess that was match point, little one.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.570
Are you satisfied now, you jerk?!

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:27.340
Mr. Hayami, I used to think that you were a respectable man, but I'm disgusted by your conduct.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.150
You are no gentleman!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:30.940
Maya!

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:36.350
I definitely want to see your play, Mr. Kuronuma.

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:38.010
Please send me an invitation.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:41.570
It's a shame this play won't be participating in the Festival.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:43.130
What was the reason for its exclusion?

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.350
Mr. Kuronuma!

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.930
Mr. Kuronuma!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.900
Maya really is something.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:54.050
<i>Isadora</i> was swept away.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:56.380
I want to go up against you as soon as possible!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.020
How could this happen?

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.790
She really bit me hard.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.510
Shiori!

00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:26.080
I'm sure that little display shocked you.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:31.360
Not in the least. You're not the type of person who does things without thinking.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.100
Shiori.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:38.060
Yes, this is the Ugetsu Agency.

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:39.950
We have another inquiry.

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:41.240
The opening night is already sold out;

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.850
and we have tons of press covering the event!

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.140
We can't handle all this hype.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:48.560
It's a call from the Acting Festival's Executive Committee.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.560
Yes, Kuronuma here.

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.540
I never thought it would get like this.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:58.950
Oden (Soup)

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.910
I'm sorry I called you out here.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.920
It's not a problem.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.350
Please, have a drink. I'm buying.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.270
Has something good happened?

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.780
Some of the Festival judges are coming to watch the play,

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.810
even though we weren't accepted into the Festival lineup.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.720
And our tickets are selling like hotcakes.

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.110
Well, that's really...

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:24.500
You know it's all because of you.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:28.090
You started that fight with Kitajima for exactly that reason, didn't you?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:33.590
Maybe. But it's her ability that made this happen.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:37.480
If her acting hadn't been as good as it was, it wouldn't have come to this.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.870
What are you planning?

00:19:41.430 --> 00:19:42.510
Nothing.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:46.820
I just hate to see talent bury its head in the sand.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:52.970
Whether it's the agency's Yuu Sakurakouji, Maya Kitajima... or yourself.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:55.160
I see. So, I also qualify as a valuable item to you?

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.960
That's rich!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.830
I've done my research on you.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:03.150
What shows you worked with, what staff you put together...

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:07.140
I researched every last bit of data from your time as a student up to the present day.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.130
Why would you do something like that?

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.400
I'll tell you after I watch your next show.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:17.260
By the way, how's the wolf girl doing?

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:20.820
She's even wilder since she bit you.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:25.300
Well, she's a contender for the role of the Scarlet Angel, after all.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:30.480
The Scarlet Angel... Well, I can understand your fixation now.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:34.700
If you can resurrect that role, your name will go down in the annals of theater history.

00:20:35.370 --> 00:20:37.170
Thank you for the drink.

00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:42.880
The contenders for the Scarlet Angel aren't just the actors, you know.

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.680
Thank you, Captain Obvious.

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.820
What? Me?

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:54.820
A contender for directing <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>?

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:58.350
This is an invitation.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:00.180
Please pass it on to Mr. Hayami.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:01.600
I promised I'd give him one.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.310
Why don't you give it to him yourself?

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.220
Are you still angry about what happened the other day?

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:09.610
I won't forget it as long as I live!

00:21:10.260 --> 00:21:12.540
But look what came of it!

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:16.220
Some of the Festival judges will be coming to see the play.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:20.680
Which means you may even be considered as a contender for an award in the Festival.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:25.110
Mr. Masumi doesn't do anything without having a reason for doing it.

00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.680
What are you talking about?

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:31.780
So, you mean he knew this would happen? But then, why?

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:34.090
Think about it.

00:21:34.430 --> 00:21:35.560
Miss Mizuki!

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:39.120
You might glimpse the truth if you consider his actions!

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:42.990
The truth? Does she mean...

00:21:44.340 --> 00:21:47.380
that he did this for me?

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:49.620
That's ridiculous.

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello hello

00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:56.680
Hello, hello.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Fukanou dato iwarenagara tobitatte

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:15.280
Even though they say it's impossible, I fly off.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
Kanaeta yume mo koboreochita yume mo aru

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:25.160
There are dreams that come true, and dreams that crumble away.

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
Soredemo isshoukenmei ikiru kazu dake hoshi ga fueru

00:22:25.160 --> 00:22:36.830
But even then, for every person trying hard to live their life, a new star is born.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Kyou mo mata hitotsu umareru hoshi miagete

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:49.240
Today, I look up again, at another newly born star.

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:50.570
And I say,

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello hello another star

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.890
Hello, hello another star.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:57.030
If I wish anything will change.

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
Ai wo daite norikonda shatoru

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:02.770
I've boarded the shuttle with my love.

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Daremo ga hitori no uchuuhikoushi dayo

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:09.120
Every single person is an astronaut.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
Negau yume kara yume e

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:14.190
From fulfilled dream to dream,

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
Dokomademo yukeru one life

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:21.470
I can go anywhere... One life.

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.510
It's finally the opening night for <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>.

00:23:26.510 --> 00:23:30.750
Mr. Purple Roses promised he'd come as well.

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:38.620
I'll give it my all... Not for the Festival judges nor for anyone else, but for you!

00:23:39.110 --> 00:23:46.900
But, an unexpected typhoon hit and the only person that braved it was...

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:48.580
you?!

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 43 - The Forgotten Wilderness
